# =============================================================================
# training/.gitignore — keeps data, checkpoints, and large artifacts out of git
# =============================================================================
#
# Description:
#   Enforces agents.md → Training code: never commit raw or processed datasets,
#   checkpoints, or large ONNX files. Shipped model files live in
#   public/models/enparse-tagger/, outside training/.
#
# Phase: 0 — Environment setup (layout creation).
#
# Tasks:
#   1. Ignore all of data/ (raw UD files, processed datasets, checkpoints,
#      TensorBoard runs, ONNX exports — see configs/data.yaml for subpaths).
#   2. Ignore model weight files anywhere under training/.
#   3. Ignore Python environment and tool caches.
#
# Dependencies:
#   Root .gitignore already ignores node_modules/ and logs.
#   Paths referenced: configs/data.yaml (data subdirectories).
# =============================================================================

# Datasets, checkpoints, logs, exports
data/

# Model weights
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt

# Python environment and caches
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
